course: dictionary
lesson: 7864
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Railway is one of them. In «Think of a toy train set next to a real railway», the railway is the track that real trains run on, because the toy set is being compared to it.
explain: «Electricity from overhead railway wires can jump to you, so you never climb on anything near them.» Here railway describes the wires that run above the trains, and the warning tells you to stay well away. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then try it in place of the word.
explain: Phrases help too. «Toad sees the red and green lights of a railway station» tells you that a railway station is a place where trains stop. The word before station shows what kind of station it is.
fact: A railway is a track made of metal rails for trains to run on.
fact: A railway can also mean the whole system of trains, tracks and stations, and the company that runs it.
fact: Railway line, railway station, railway crossing and model railway are common phrases.
fact: «If something falls onto the railway tracks, you never climb down; you tell a member of staff.»
fact: Never play on or near a railway line. Only cross at a proper railway crossing.
exercise: «Think of a toy train set next to a real railway.» In this sentence, what is a railway? | A station where people wait | A kind of toy train | *A track made of metal rails for trains to run on | A type of lorry
exercise: «Electricity from overhead railway wires can jump to you.» What is the safe choice? | *Keep away from anything near the railway wires | Hold the wires to test them | Play on the railway line | Climb up to touch the wires
exercise: Which phrase names a place where trains stop? | *A railway station | A railway crossing | A railway line | A model railway
test: «If something falls onto the railway tracks, what should you do?» | Climb down and pick it up | *Tell a member of staff | Shout for your friends to help | Stand very still and wait
test: In the phrase model railway, what does railway mean? | A bus route through the town | A school trip by coach | A real train company | *A track for toy trains
exam: What does railway mean when it means the whole system? | A toy for young children | A bridge over a river | A single metal rail | *The trains, tracks and stations together, and the company that runs them
